---
import BaseLayout from "../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | FTFN">
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Civilization is a choice.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      FTFN is a future-state intelligence project at ftfn.io. It tracks what could
      be, what that future depends on, and which constraints may decide whether it arrives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section prose">
    <h2>Editorial Posture</h2>
    <p>
      FTFN is curious, skeptical, urgent, and imaginative. It summarizes claims,
      names who is making them, identifies dependencies, and connects signals to
      the local systems that can turn information into outcomes.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial Method</h2>
    <p>
      FTFN starts with the original source, separates claims from evidence,
      places each signal on the maturity ladder, and names the dependencies and
      constraints that decide whether a future can scale.
    </p>
    <h2>Source Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      Official data, research findings, company announcements, credible
      reporting, and speculative claims are treated differently. Company claims
      stay labeled as interested-party evidence until stronger support exists.
    </p>
    <h2>Publication Standard</h2>
    <p>
      Draft sample records are scaffolding. Published records should have
      reviewed sources, defensible evidence labels, clear uncertainty language,
      and visible paths back to the original source.
    </p>
    <p>
      The detailed method, publication gate, and correction posture now live on
      the <a href="/method/">Method and Publication Policy</a> page.
    </p>
    <h2>Core Thesis</h2>
    <p>
      The future is not a list of inventions. It is a stack of dependencies.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
